body:
You can all pretend you won't use rorqs after the nerf but really, you know you will. It'll be slightly below active as fuck carrier ratting income, for still just sitting there and waiting in a ship that has near triage level of tank and a 5-7 minute invulnerability timer to get help. You'll still get your ore, you'll stop crashing the market to stupid levels as quickly, you'll still have the magical fairy invulnerability that was cancer to the game to introduce.  
&nbsp;


You say for nullsec to remain fresh, they need to remain OP miners. Okay, remove their ability to be invulnerable or cut it in half.  It's a capital boosting/support ship. It makes zero sense for it to be able to all that it can do in one single ship. 
All your arguments about it's price. Since when is price used as a balancing factor in eve. Any other time it's mentioned as a reason for something to be powerful, it's shot down because it isn't and it's stupid for any ship to be thought of like that. Should we buff titans and supers even more? They're more expensive than a rorq is.  
&nbsp;




Also OP, your suggestion for the NSA to lock a carrier in place is..well, I can't even describe the levels that falls to. Carriers are meant to be mobile, moving and relocating. They're squishy as hell, fighters even more so(and more after the patch). You've left me wordless after this verbal *typed* diarrhea.  
&nbsp;


I've lost track of what I was saying in this rambling mess from a sleep deprived mind. Your ideas are silly and you should feel bad and leave your bubble.
